# Visual presentation (ISO 9241-125, ISO/IEC 25010)

## Harmony and balance
- One spacing scale (e.g. 4/8/12/16/24/32/48). Same padding on comparable regions.
- Align to a grid. Do not mix leftover margins.
- Type: clear hierarchy (page title → section → body → meta). Consistent weights and line-height. Reading order is visual order.
- Density: spacious dashboard cards (24px radius). Tables live inside cards. One soft shadow on surfaces, not stacked chrome.

## Information architecture
- Label sits with its control (not a distant table header only). Related actions group together.
- Tokens only: background, surface, text, text-muted, line, accent, danger, success, warning. No one-off hex in components.
- Every interactive component has **default, hover, focus, active, disabled, loading, empty, error**. If a state exists in logic, it is visible.

## Contrast and perception
- See `wcag-aa.mdc`. Status is never color alone (icon + text).
- Focus ring is visible. Touch targets 44×44px on worker phones; never under 24×24px.
